      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Twenty-four hours after the ingestion of black grouper, lower-extremity paresthesias, left retrobulbar pain, pruritus, diarrhea, and urinary frequency developed in a 57-year-old woman. Over a three-month period, her symptoms gradually resolved completely. A review of the systemic and neuro-ophthalmologic manifestations of ciguatera poisoning is presented."},
